LOCATION_FRAMING = {
 'Extreme wide':'A very distant establishing composition. Show the complete place and a broad surrounding landscape; the principal building occupies only a small part of the frame. Emphasize environmental scale.',
 'Wide':'A wide architectural establishing view showing the complete main space, its floor or ground, ceiling or sky and surroundings, with clear foreground and background depth.',
 'Close-up':'An architectural detail fills the frame: a small part of one doorway, decorative carving, window or material junction. Crop away most of the building and surroundings. Show the requested place through an intimate detail.',
 'Low angle':'Camera at ground height, tilted clearly upward into the architecture. Exaggerated rising verticals, visible undersides of overhead structures and towering walls; very little ground is visible.',
 'High angle':'Camera high above the space, looking diagonally downward. Floor layout, rooftops or ground planes dominate; show top surfaces rather than an eye-level facade.',
 'Aerial':'A distant elevated oblique aerial view looking down across the whole location and its surrounding terrain, with clearly readable roofs and paths.',
 'Dutch angle':'Roll the entire camera about 25 degrees. The architectural verticals and horizon lean conspicuously together; retain coherent perspective, not deformed buildings.',
 'Frame within a frame':'View the location through a nearby dark archway, doorway or window that surrounds the image edges. Keep that foreground frame visible and the space beyond readable.',
 'Symmetrical':'Camera exactly centered on the architectural axis, facing straight forward. Strong one-point perspective and balanced mirrored geometry on both sides.',
 'Negative space':'Place the main architecture in one outer third of the composition, with a large quiet empty sky or plain ground occupying the remaining two thirds.',
 'Deep staging':'Strong layered architectural composition: a large nearby object at an edge, a readable central space in the midground and a distant opening beyond. Show clear depth separation between all three layers.',
}
